      "jobId": "66b05c0c-a5e1-402a-aa1d-69415338c9be",
      "prompt": "Close-up of an arched stone road tunnel portal set into the raised face of a grassy hillside on a diorama tile, on a plain neutral grey studio backdrop: a head wall of rough-faced blocks of weathered pale grey granite speckled with darker grey flecks, with a few warm buff fieldstones among them, laid in neat level courses in pale lime mortar, every block a little irregular with softly worn rounded edges and its own slight tone, patches of pale green-grey and mustard-yellow lichen, dark green moss in the joints and thickest along the foot of the wall, and faint darker rain streaks running down from under the coping, the stone reading as a matte surface, an elliptical arch over a two-lane asphalt country road with low concrete kerbs and a faded dashed centre line, the arch ringed by a bold band of pale dressed granite voussoirs with crisp chamfered edges and a slightly larger projecting keystone at the crown, standing on squared dressed jamb stones, a pale dressed granite coping with a small projecting drip edge along the top of the wall, the meadow turf of the hill runs over the top of the wall and its long grass and a few small ferns tumble over the front edge of the coping, and the steep banks of the road cutting are lush and uneven, with grass tufts, a few wildflowers, small ferns and dock leaves growing up against the foot of the wall, the opening a shadowed recess whose stone soffit fades to near-black a short way inside, with no view through, and a pair of small black iron wall lanterns with warm amber glass panes, a little rust at their seams, each hung from a curled wrought-iron bracket fixed to the wall either side of the arch, rich specific surface detail. The whole portal is a clean photoreal 3D computer graphics render, stylized-real diorama miniature, real PBR materials, slightly exaggerated proportions, soft noon sun, neutral grey studio background, 35 degree three-quarter view"
    },
